15 0 obj
<< /A 51 0 R /Alt (Flowchart illustrating an underwater image detection system pipeline, beginning with RGB image input and passing through modules for feature reweighting, frequency-aware attention, and query adaptation using transformer encoding, ending with object detection results and loss computations for classification, localization, and matching.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 52 0 R /Alt (Flowchart illustrating a frequency reweighting process for image tensors, where frequency masks are generated and combined into a reweight matrix, applied in the frequency domain via fast Fourier transforms, before inverse transformation and extraction of real values.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 53 0 R /Alt (Diagram illustrates a neural network architecture with multi-scale convolutions \(conv 5×5, 7×7, 9×9\) fused via mean fusion, followed by frequency-aware weighting, gating with sigmoid, dropout, and an output summation.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 37 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 54 0 R /Alt (Diagram showing the process of per-query scalar reweighting in a neural network. Input queries arranged as a blue three-dimensional block are multiplied by query-specific scales from a learnable logit vector after bounded scale mapping and reshaping. The output queries appear as a green three-dimensional block, representing scaled queries. Mathematical expressions for bounded scale mapping and conceptual reweighting are shown in annotated callouts.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 39 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 55 0 R /Alt (Horizontal bar chart comparing the number of instances across 22 classes such as trash types, animal categories, plant, and rov, with trash_unknown_instance and rov exhibiting the highest counts, measured along the x-axis labeled Number of Instances.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 40 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 56 0 R /Alt (Four scatter plots compare object detection models: Faster RCNN, SSD, YOLO variants, RT-DETR, and RF-DETR. Top left \(A\): GFLOPs vs mAP@50 shows RF-DETR with high mAP@50 and moderate GFLOPs. Top right \(B\): GFLOPs vs F1 displays RF-DETR with the highest F1 and efficiency. Bottom left \(C\): Parameters vs mAP@50 shows RF-DETR achieving high mAP@50 with fewer parameters. Bottom right \(D\): Parameters vs F1 depicts RF-DETR with the top F1 score and lower parameter count. Each legend identifies models by symbol and color.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 43 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
21 0 obj
<< /A 57 0 R /Alt (Eight underwater camera images show comparisons between manual and automated marine object detection. Each image pair highlights boxes and labels for trash and animal instances with confidence scores, using color-coded rectangles to indicate detected, missed, or categorized objects.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 44 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
22 0 obj
<< /A 58 0 R /Alt (Grid of underwater scene images in five columns and six rows, where the top row shows original images and the remaining rows display heatmap visualizations from different detection models and combinations, comparing localization performance of RF-DETR, UFFR+MFA, UFFR+QAR, MFA+QAR, and Improved RF-DETR.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 45 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
23 0 obj
<< /A 59 0 R /Alt (Comparison of underwater video frames across five object detection models\204YOLOv11n, RT-DETR, YOLO26n, YOLO26s, and Improved RF-DETR\204displayed in rows beneath the original images. Each column presents a different underwater scene, while colored bounding boxes highlight detected objects such as trash containers and starfish, with accompanying labels and confidence scores annotated for each model\220s predictions.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 46 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
24 0 obj
<< /A 60 0 R /Alt (Four grouped stacked bar charts compare YOLO and RT-DETR model performance across twenty object categories for precision, mean average precision at fifty percent and fifty to ninety-five percent, and recall, with color-coded legend distinguishing models and visible variation in results per category and metric.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 48 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
